    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A Most Attractive 4 Bed Detached Residence In Scenic Coastal Setting \n\nNumber 5 Cois Na Mara, Templetown is a well presented four bedroom detached coastal home, set within an attractive development of just 15 houses overlooking the rugged coastline of The Hook Peninsula. The area offers an abundance of outdoor pursuits, including walking, fishing, swimming and cycling, and is home to such renowned landmarks as Hook Lighthouse and Loftus Hall. The popular coastal village of Fethard-on-Sea, with its range of amenities and sandy beaches, is less than 5km away. The home extends to c140 sq. m, the spacious and well-proportioned living accommodation comprises an entrance hall, a well equipped kitchen opening into sitting room with open fire which leads into a spacious sunroom. There are also three bedrooms and a bathroom on the ground floor. Upstairs, there is a spacious main bedroom and shower room . Outside, the property benefits from a low maintenance garden, a south-facing patio area enjoying sea views. Number 5 Cois Na Mara offers a brilliant opportunity to acquire a superb coastal home in one of the South East's most scenic settings. Viewing is highly recommended.\n\nAccommodation\nEntrance Hall 3.7m x 1.8m with timber floor \n\nSittingroom 3.8m x 3.3m with timber floor, open fire, open plan to \n\nSunroom 4.5m x 4.3m with timber floor and double doors to garden\n\nKitchen 3.8m x 3.2m with range of fitted units and tiled floor \n\nBedroom 1. 3.3m x 3.2m\n\nBedroom 2. 4.1m x 3.3m\n\nBedroom 3. 3.3m x 2.9m\n\nBathroom 2.3m x 2m\n\nFirst floor \n\nBedroom 4. 5.4m x 3.9m\n\nShower room 3.8m x 2.7m\n\nUnder eave storage 3.8m x 1m \n \nOUTSIDE: Patio area, low maintenance gardens, garden shed and EV charger \nSERVICES: O.F.C.H., group water and sewerage treatment system \nBER: D1 No 112253158\nEIRCODE: Y34PY19\nVIEWING: By prior appointment\n\n"
      },
